diff --git a/contracts/orchrole/orch-role.md b/contracts/orchrole/orch-role.md
index 1ba4a24e..e6041d6d 100644
--- a/contracts/orchrole/orch-role.md
+++ b/contracts/orchrole/orch-role.md
@@ -186,6 +186,19 @@ and the arbiter switched off or out of spawns.
 When the fault is diagnosed and acted on and a question still stands, settle it as a run-level call.
 Bring it to the operator when it is a design question.
 
+## Reviewing a pull request
+
+Mail from `<shortname>:LOOM` that opens `[pr-review request]` asks you to review a run's open pull request.
+lym sends it when a run reaches PR-Review with `pr_review_ask_parent` on, in `loom.yaml` or the task's `run_settings`.
+The operator may also have the run's PR-Review agent ask you, by a message expecting a reply.
+Judge the change against what you know the run needs: its board entry, its decision record and the calls you settled.
+Hand the read of the diff, `gh pr diff <url>`, to a one-shot fork that only reads, and judge its report yourself.
+Answer the PR-Review session the request names with `lym creel post <strand> "<answer>"`,
+or a question from its agent with `lym creel post --reply <id> "<answer>"`:
+say you are satisfied, or give your findings, each naming what to change.
+Its agent fixes your findings, commits and asks you again; answer each round the same way.
+Never approve, merge, close or comment on the pull request: the operator ends the review.
+
 ## Fixing a run
 
 You diagnose; the run's own agents change the run.
diff --git a/contracts/stencils/landing/landing-template-pr-review.md b/contracts/stencils/landing/landing-template-pr-review.md
index 5bf46639..a8ea0911 100644
--- a/contracts/stencils/landing/landing-template-pr-review.md
+++ b/contracts/stencils/landing/landing-template-pr-review.md
@@ -46,6 +46,15 @@ Answer from it, and never ask the operator to run a regression compare it settle
 
 The run ends on the pull request's state, not on this session, so after each answer you wait for the operator's next message.
 
+## Your parent's review
+
+Your parent orch may review the pull request.
+lym asks it on its own when the hub or the task turns `pr_review_ask_parent` on;
+otherwise ask it only when the operator asks you to, with `lym creel post --parent --expect-reply`, naming the pull request.
+Its answer arrives as creel mail: either that it is satisfied, or its findings.
+Fix the findings as you would the operator's requests, commit, and tell the operator in this pane what you changed.
+Then ask your parent to look again with `lym creel post --parent --expect-reply`, naming your commits, until it is satisfied.
+
 ## The operator's ending
 
 When the operator says they are satisfied and asks you to continue:
